    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6388" root="جن" body-key="j">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَنِينٌ</span></b>  Anything <i>veiled, concealed, hidden,</i> or
<i>covered:</i> (K:) applied as an epithet even to
rancour, or malice. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>Buried; deposited
in a grave.</i> (IDrd, S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>An embryo; a fœtus;
the child,</i> or <i>young, in the belly;</i> (S Msb, K;)
[i. e.,] <i>in the womb:</i> (Mgh:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجِنَّةٌ</span> (S, Msb,
K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجْنُنٌ</span>. (ISd, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And the former of
these pls., <i>Waters choked up with earth.</i> (TA.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَنَنٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also The <i>vulva.</i> (TA.)

